# SpeedTestCard: at the bottom of the Wi-Fi menu; button at the card's right edge. Both looks.
ipc panels open wifiMenu IRICE-TEST
wait 2
shot card
note Speed test card at the bottom of the menu: button "Test speed" (Material: filled primary 32 px pill; Glass: accent 28 px). Same as QML.
# NOTE: button position is read from the shot; assumed near the menu's bottom right. click on layer surfaces may not register in the harness
ptr move 1780 420 sleep 300 glide 1780 420 100 sleep 300
shot hover
note Hovering the button: Material 8 % state layer in 150 ms; Glass subtle hover tint. Same as QML.
rec net-press 0.6 ptr move 1780 420 sleep 100 down sleep 400 up
note Material: corners to 8 in about 0.22 s with a slight overshoot, button swells about 6 %. Glass: shrinks to 97 % in 100 ms with no overshoot. Compare QML vs Rust frame strips. (position assumed; adjust if the button is elsewhere)
wait 1
shot after
note Without network: pressing starts a test that ends in an error; the button reads "Test again" (error state), same text as QML. With network the figures update live without flicker.
# MANUAL: with network: click -> "Cancel" (tonal), figures update live; record 2 s and check the stats row does not blink
ipc panels close
